# TEMPLATE. Client-side entry for the headless EC2 agent box, reached over
# Tailscale. setup/desktop-links.sh COPIES this file to
# ~/.ssh/config.d/agentbox.conf the first time it runs, and never touches
# that copy again -- edit your copy, not this template, so your edits
# survive re-running bootstrap and never dirty the repo.
# Requires `Include config.d/*` as the first line of ~/.ssh/config.
#
# NOTE: ssh_config comments must be on their own line. A trailing comment
# after a directive is not reliably supported and can fail to parse, so keep
# the notes above the lines they describe rather than beside them.
#
# Three CHANGEME values to replace in your copy:
#
#   HostName      the box's MagicDNS name, which server-tailscale.sh prints
#                 when it finishes. Plain `tailscale status` does NOT show the
#                 tailnet suffix, only the short name and the 100.x IP; the
#                 full name is `tailscale status --json | jq -r .Self.DNSName`.
#                 The bare short name and the 100.x IP both work here too --
#                 see the readme.
#   User          whatever login the instance was provisioned with. Debian
#                 cloud images default to `admin`; creating a differently-named
#                 user is instance provisioning, not this repo's job. The
#                 server-side setup scripts are username-agnostic, so this line
#                 is the only place the choice has to be recorded.
#   IdentityFile  the key that authenticates YOU TO THE BOX -- usually the EC2
#                 keypair the instance was launched with (a .pem, mode 400).
#                 DELETE THE LINE ENTIRELY if your default key (~/.ssh/id_ed25519
#                 or id_rsa) already gets you in. Do not leave the CHANGEME
#                 path in place: ssh warns on every connection about an
#                 identity file it cannot read.
#
# IdentityFile is unrelated to ForwardAgent below. This key logs you in to the
# box; the forwarded agent is what lets git ON the box push to GitHub as you.
# You generally want both, and neither substitutes for the other.

Host agentbox
  HostName agentbox.CHANGEME.ts.net
  User CHANGEME
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/CHANGEME
  # Uncomment if login fails with "Too many authentication failures": a
  # loaded agent offers every key it holds before this one and the box
  # cuts the connection at MaxAuthTries. This restricts the attempt to
  # the IdentityFile above.
  # IdentitiesOnly yes
  ForwardAgent yes
  ServerAliveInterval 30
  ServerAliveCountMax 6
